          "citation": "2016 CO 39",
          "court": "Supreme Court of Colorado",
          "year": 2016,
          "date_decided": "2016-05-23",
          "holding": "The court held that neither the injurious-environment provision of section 19-3-102(1)(c) nor Troxel requires the State to prove parental fault, or to prove that both parents lack the availability, ability and willingness to provide reasonable parental care, before a child may be adjudicated dependent or neglected.",
          "relevance": "This is the controlling Colorado statement of what the State must prove to obtain an adjudication after a petition is filed, and of what it need not prove.",
          "quote": "We hold that the statute does not require the jury to make findings of parental fault",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4247582/people-in-the-interest-of-jg/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 4247582
        },
