          "case_name": "People in Interest of S.N. v. S.N.",
          "citation": "2014 CO 64, 329 P.3d 276",
          "court": "Supreme Court of Colorado",
          "year": 2014,
          "date_decided": "2014-06-30",
          "holding": "The court held that whether a child is dependent and neglected because of prospective harm is a mixed question of law and fact, so summary judgment in such adjudications is neither always available nor always barred and must be evaluated case by case on whether the material evidentiary facts are undisputed.",
          "relevance": "It governs how a prospective-harm dependency petition may be resolved short of trial.",
          "quote": "We hold that courts must evaluate whether summary judgment is appropriate in a dependency and neglect adjudication involving prospective harm on a case-by-case basis.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/5344629/people-ex-rel-sn-v-sn/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 5344629
        }
